# Every layer a remainder walk passes through rather than stops on. One row per row of
# composition/remainder_frontier.sqlc whose layer composition/unsettled.sqlc names.
#
# The other half of the difference
#   The frontier's rows are either stopping points or layers the walk continued through.
#   composition/settled_remainders.sqlc is the first half, the frontier less the unsettled layers,
#   and this is the second, the frontier kept to them. A layer passed through carries no remainder
#   up; what it contributes is its own elimination, which composition/carried_eliminations.sqlc
#   carries, and any ground that suspends it, for which composition/suspended_remainders.sqlc
#   suspends the remainder above it.
#
# Every path, usable or not
#   Kept here whatever the path's `usable` says, because a suspension at a layer the walk reaches
#   suspends the remainder above it whether or not the path's product is known. A reader that adds
#   up along the path keeps to `usable` itself.
#
# Checked by
#   algebra/settled_remainders.sqlc holds the usable frontier to its three groups: this, the
#   settled rows, and the stops with no figure.
-- composition/remainder_frontier.sqlc restricted to the nodes composition/unsettled.sqlc names.
SELECT w.*
FROM      (
    :compose(composition/remainder_frontier.sqlc)
) w
JOIN      (
    :compose(composition/unsettled.sqlc)
) u ON u.filing = w.filing AND u.layer = w.layer
